                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40cceae9-5c26-37a5-b9dc-3f5be9d4e44c",
                                        "entry_id": "665b4e52-a5fb-3ffe-be0d-2918482d4cad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person given to excess in the consumption of food and drink; a greedy or ravenous eater."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98b9015f-6642-4eb5-8c60-f0fc00b1c40f",
                                                "sense_id": "40cceae9-5c26-37a5-b9dc-3f5be9d4e44c",
                                                "text": "I knew him, at Caivs trencher, when for hyre, / He proſtituted his abuſed body / To that great gourmond, fat Apicivs;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6850d1a-2d3c-495b-86b6-f4ecab747eeb",
                                                "sense_id": "40cceae9-5c26-37a5-b9dc-3f5be9d4e44c",
                                                "text": "The colonel and his sponsor made a queer contrast: Greystone [the sponsor] long and stringy, with a face that seemed as if a cold wind was eternally playing on it. […] But there was not a more lascivious reprobate and gourmand in all London than this same Greystone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a05caa91-a6b2-3eeb-82bd-48dc1500f960",
                                        "entry_id": "665b4e52-a5fb-3ffe-be0d-2918482d4cad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who appreciates good food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa55b460-2e6c-4e05-b08a-5d5c72af98e7",
                                                "sense_id": "a05caa91-a6b2-3eeb-82bd-48dc1500f960",
                                                "text": "The third key was the number of demands from different patrons or groups for their own specialized cuisines. Such patrons included the court, rich households, and scholar-gourmands. Buddhists and Muslims also elaborated their own cuisines (sucai 素菜 and qingzhen 清真)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
